# Target A: triangle-core tube plus zero-slack source rank cap

Date: 2026-10-03
Base main: 6c45398dcfe69e3b3bb322920a2911468dfe0573
Status: proof-only candidate, noncanonical. Target A and Level I remain open.

This is separate from the active Target B four-bar case-2 route and Worker-B's finite
nine-no-root k=6 route. It treats the simultaneous Target A branch where the
Section-168 zero-slack source endpoint exists and the actual response optimum has the
Section-172 locked three-channel fan.

## 1. One-sided source-shell defect

If K is convex with perimeter P and X is a unit-separated subset of K, let X_w be the
points at distance at most w from the boundary. Open radius-1/2 disks about X_w are
disjoint and lie in (K+B_(1/2)) minus K_-(w+1/2). Steiner plus inner coarea gives

    |X_w| <= 4(w+1)P/pi + 1.

Since P <= pi diam(K),

    |X_1| <= 8 diam(K)+1.                                  (1)

For the actual response optimum X* in K*, diameter d, any response point whose
zero-slack source partner lies outside K* is within distance below one of the boundary.
Thus there are at most 8d+1 such response points.

## 2. Contact lenses contain at most two source labels

For a unit contact pq put L(pq)=B(p,1) intersect B(q,1). Any unit-separated set has
at most two points in L(pq). Normalize p=(-1/2,0), q=(1/2,0). In the upper half-lens,
with r=(0,sqrt(3)/2), the lens inequalities imply

    |z-r|^2 < 2-sqrt(1-y^2)-sqrt(3)y <= 1.

So the upper half-lens lies in a unit Reuleaux triangle and has strict diameter below
one; the lower half is the reflected case. Hence at most one unit-separated point lies
in each half.

An off-shield strict source arm c-a meeting a contact shield Sigma cannot pass through
a shield vertex, because that would put a distinct X* point within distance below one
of c. It therefore properly crosses some unit contact edge pq. Section-177 crossing
geometry puts a in L(pq). Injectivity gives

    source arms crossing Sigma <= 2|E(Sigma)|.             (2)

## 3. Active sink cap

Take independently the Section-177.5 zero-slack matchings
M_C:C^partial->A0 and M_O:O->A0, and let L be their common-source count. Section
177.5A gives

    L >= |C^partial|+|O|-20d-25.                           (3)

Let B_C=C^partial intersect widehat W_Sigma, b=|B_C|, and retain the Section-175
sets T_O,O_iso,C_i,O_i. Then sum_i|C_i|=|C^partial|-b.

Call a common-source gate exceptional if its C endpoint is in B_C, its source lies
outside K*, its source arm crosses Sigma, or its O endpoint lies in T_O. By (1), (2),
and injectivity, there are at most

    b+(8d+1)+2|E(Sigma)|+|T_O|                             (4)

exceptional gates.

Every nonexceptional gate either ends at O_iso or is sector-preserving C_i-A0-O_i.
If its source a and a surviving response neighbor x of o were in different sectors,
[a,x] would cross Sigma. Both lie in the open unit disk B(o,1), forcing o into T_O,
a contradiction. Therefore

    L <= b+8d+1+2|E(Sigma)|+|T_O|+|O_iso|
         +sum_i min(|C_i|,|O_i|).                          (5)

Using sum_i min <= sum_i|C_i| and
|O|=|T_O|+|O_iso|+sum_i|O_i|, comparison with (3) yields

    sum_i|O_i| <= 2|E(Sigma)|+28d+26.                      (6)

Section 175.3 then gives

    rank S <= |T_Sigma|+2|E(Sigma)|+28d+26.                (7)

## 4. Triangle-core pointwise Voronoi tube

Assume Sigma is connected and contains the boundary of a unit equilateral triangle P.
Let V_phi be the centered Voronoi hexagon of a rotated unit triangular lattice and
K_phi=V_phi+B_1. Then

    area(V_phi)=sqrt(3)/2,
    per(V_phi)=2sqrt(3),
    area(K_phi)=5sqrt(3)/2+pi,
    w_K(n)=w_V(n)+2.                                       (8)

For every translation, each lattice site y with dist(y,|Sigma|)<1 has its full
Voronoi cell in |Sigma|+K_phi, so

    |T_Sigma| sqrt(3)/2 <= area(|Sigma|+K_phi).             (9)

Start from the filled triangle P, which only enlarges the shield. For centrally
symmetric K, the polygon mixed-area formula is

    area(P+K)=area(P)+area(K)
              +(1/2)sum_(triangle edges e) w_K(n_e).       (10)

Order remaining contact edges so each shares an endpoint with the exposed graph.
Adding a unit edge e increases the enclosing Minkowski area by at most w_K(n_e).
With E=|E(Sigma)|,

    area(|Sigma|+K_phi)
    <= area(K_phi)+sqrt(3)/4+2E-3
       +(1/2)sum_triangle w_Vphi(n_e)
       +sum_nontriangle w_Vphi(n_e).                       (11)

The regular-hexagon width is pi/3-periodic and has rotational mean
per(V)/pi=2sqrt(3)/pi. The weighted edge count in (11) is E-3/2. Therefore one
rotation phi_* satisfies

    (1/2)sum_triangle w_Vphi*(n_e)+sum_nontriangle w_Vphi*(n_e)
    <= (2sqrt(3)/pi)(E-3/2).                               (12)

Section 154 permits a prescribed rotated and translated response lattice. After fixing
phi_*, (9)-(12) hold for every translation, so a generic translation can be chosen.
Dividing by sqrt(3)/2 gives

    |T_Sigma| <= floor(
        (4/sqrt(3)+4/pi)E
        +11/2+2pi/sqrt(3)-2sqrt(3)-6/pi).                  (13)

The edge coefficient is 3.582640621493666... and the additive constant is
3.753637796227936....

## 5. Locked-fan consequence

For the Section-172 locked fan, E=V=:v. Combining (7) and (13),

    rank S
    <= floor((4/sqrt(3)+4/pi)v
             +11/2+2pi/sqrt(3)-2sqrt(3)-6/pi)
       +2v+28d+26.                                         (14)

Thus the simultaneous zero-slack/locked subbranch closes whenever

    |C^partial|-s
    >= floor((4/sqrt(3)+4/pi)v
             +11/2+2pi/sqrt(3)-2sqrt(3)-6/pi)
       +2v+28d+26.                                         (15)

The effective fan coefficient is 2+4/sqrt(3)+4/pi =
5.582640621493666..., instead of 11 when the same source classification is paired
with current-main's 9v pointwise tube estimate.

All claims are analytic. No finite search, verifier, CI output, or heuristic is a
premise. Target A remains open. The residual task is to prove that |C^partial|-s pays
the right side of (15), or to replace one of the linear currencies by a strict sub-D
competitor. The zero-slack branch with triangle-free actual response and the locked
branch without the zero-slack source endpoint remain unresolved.
